	"ok meanness  -  plain      Me-2   The weak are safe beside me. I save what is hard in me for rulers who think their size excuses them, and there is a great deal of it saved.",
	"ok meanness  -  plain      Me-3   I do not kick what is beneath me. My quarrel is always upward, with whoever at this table believes no one can touch them.",
	"ok meanness  -  bedrock    Me-B1  I have no taste for bullying the small and I despise the rulers who do. It is the strong I want to see brought down, and the stronger they are the more I want it and the less I care what it costs.",
	"ok meanness  -  bedrock    Me-B2  The weak are safe beside me, and whoever preys on them is not. Everything hard in me is kept for the crown that thinks itself beyond reach.",
	"ok meanness  ~  fault      Me~1   One sees a weak neighbour's land as land lying open; the other has no taste for the small and wants only the strong brought down.",
	"ok meanness  ~  fault      Me~2   Half of me is tempted by everything that cannot defend itself; the other half despises that hunger and turns it on whoever stands tallest.",
	"ok meanness  \077  unwritten  Me\0771   I do not know yet what a weak neighbour is to me: someone to shelter, or land lying open. The first I meet will teach me.",
	"ok meanness  \077  unwritten  Me\0772   I have not yet stood over anyone who could not stop me, and I do not know what I do there. Whatever I do the first time, I expect I will do again.",
	"ok meanness  +  born       Me^+   I am harder on the weak than my blood ever was. Those who shelter under my house's name should look at who wears the crown now.",
	"ok meanness  -  born       Me^-   I have less appetite for the weak than my blood had, and more for larger game. The strong who think my house troubles only the small are mistaken about their safety.",
	"ok denounce  +  plain      De+1   When I think a ruler is a liar I say so, to their face and to the whole table.",
	"ok denounce  +  plain      De+2   I do not keep my judgements to myself. What I think of a ruler everyone will know, and I want the others to choose a side.",
	"ok denounce  +  plain      De+3   I name my enemies aloud. A quarrel kept quiet is a quarrel half fought, and I want every crown at this table to hear who wronged me.",
	"ok denounce  +  bedrock    De+B1  When I think a ruler is a liar I say so, to their face and to the whole table, and I go on saying it until no one will sit beside them.",
	"ok denounce  +  bedrock    De+B2  I name my enemies aloud and early. I want the whole table to know who has wronged me, and I count the ones who heard and did nothing.",
	"ok denounce  -  plain      De-1   I keep my judgements to myself. The ruler I have condemned is the last to learn of it, and by then words are not what I am sending.",
	"ok denounce  -  plain      De-2   I do not shout across the table. I smile at those I mean to ruin, and I let them find out all at once what I thought of them.",
	"ok denounce  -  plain      De-3   Speeches against a rival are for rulers who can do nothing else. I give no warning; I would rather be misjudged than expected.",
	"ok denounce  -  bedrock    De-B1  I keep my judgements to myself and my face still. The ruler I have condemned is the very last to learn of it, and learns it from what arrives, not from anything I said.",
	"ok denounce  -  bedrock    De-B2  I never warn an enemy. I am pleasant to those I mean to ruin right up to the hour, and I think less of any ruler who announces themselves.",
	"ok denounce  ~  fault      De~1   One says what it thinks of a ruler to the whole table; the other keeps its face still and lets the condemned find out last.",
	"ok denounce  ~  fault      De~2   Half of me wants every wrong named aloud before all the crowns; the other half never warns an enemy and thinks warning is for the weak.",
	"ok denounce  \077  unwritten  De\0771   I do not know yet whether I am one who names an enemy before the whole table or one who smiles until the hour. The first ruler I come to despise will get one or the other, and the table will know me by it.",
	"ok denounce  \077  unwritten  De\0772   No one has yet earned my contempt, and I do not know what I do with it: say it to every crown, or keep it behind my teeth until it can be acted on. The first to earn it will find out.",
	"ok denounce  +  born       De^+   I speak my mind before the whole table more freely than my blood did. Those who expect a quiet neighbour will hear their names.",
	"ok denounce  -  born       De^-   I am quieter about my enemies than those before me were. The ruler who hears nothing from me should take no comfort in it.",
};
